# Testing Standards

All tests should follow these standards:

Test Organization:
- Place tests in __tests__ directory next to the code being tested
- Use .test.tsx extension for component tests
- Use .test.ts extension for utility and hook tests

Test Structure:
- Use describe blocks for grouping related tests
- Use clear it/test descriptions that explain the expected behavior
- Follow AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert
- One assertion concept per test

Testing Hooks:
- Use renderHook from @testing-library/react
- Wrap state updates in act()
- Test initial state
- Test all state updates
- Test edge cases

Example Tests:
- [src/ui/hooks/useMovies.ts/__tests__/useMovies.test.tsx](mdc:src/ui/hooks/useMovies.ts/__tests__/useMovies.test.tsx)
- [src/App.test.tsx](mdc:src/App.test.tsx)

Assertions:
- Use specific assertions over generic ones
- Test both positive and negative cases
- Test boundary conditions
- Verify correct types in TypeScript tests
